1. Why Karpenter over Cluster Autoscaler?

Answer:

Cluster Autoscaler scales pre-defined node groups (ASGs). Karpenter directly provisions the most suitable node based on pending pod requirements.

Benefits:

Faster scaling
No need to maintain multiple ASGs
Better bin-packing
Lower cloud costs
Supports Spot and On-Demand intelligently

Interview One-Liner:

Cluster Autoscaler scales node groups; Karpenter scales infrastructure dynamically based on pod requirements.

2. How does Karpenter provision nodes?

Answer:

Flow:

Plain Text
Pending Pod
↓
Scheduler cannot place Pod
↓
Karpenter observes unschedulable Pod
↓
Calculates CPU/Memory requirements
↓
Selects best EC2 instance
↓
Creates NodeClaim
↓
Launches EC2 Instance
↓
Node joins cluster
↓
Pod gets scheduled
