15. Explain a production cost optimization implemented using Karpenter

Strong Senior-Level Answer

In one environment, we migrated from Cluster Autoscaler to Karpenter on EKS. We enabled NodePools that allowed multiple EC2 instance families instead of restricting workloads to fixed node groups. For non-critical workloads such as CI/CD runners, ETL jobs, and batch processing, we used Spot capacity. We also enabled consolidation to remove underutilized nodes automatically. As load fluctuated during the day, Karpenter right-sized compute capacity and removed idle nodes, improving utilization and reducing AWS compute costs while maintaining application availability.

